2026-10-14T22:51:54.0466172Z +++ RELION: command line arguments (with defaults for optional ones between parantheses) +++
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0467069Z ====== General options ===== 
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0468094Z                                 --i : STAR file with all input micrographs, the tomography tilt series, or a Linux wildcard with all micrographs to operate on
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0469262Z                    --o (MotionCorr) : Name for the output directory
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0470045Z              --skip_logfile (false) : Skip generation of tracks-part of the logfile.pdf
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0471470Z           --skip_report_pdf (false) : Write the dataset STAR file but no logfile.pdf (for parallel workers whose report is built by a later --aggregate_only run)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0472760Z                             --j (1) : Number of threads per movie (= process)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0473729Z               --max_io_threads (-1) : Limit the number of IO threads.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0475038Z                        --profile () : Write a per-movie, per-stage wall/CPU/page-fault profile to this JSON-lines file (docs/stage_profile.md). Diagnostic; products are unchanged.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0477122Z         --profile_device_timing (1) : With --profile: 1 (default) also times CUDA steps with events, which adds host waits; 0 records the stage profile and NVTX ranges with production device synchronisation.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0478793Z               --sync_output (false) : Write output products on the main thread instead of a background writer thread (same products, same order).
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0479849Z                     --ingest (auto) : Movie ingest path: auto (default), nvcomp, compact or float. Anything but auto fails a movie that cannot use that path, instead of silently using another.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0480816Z                 --ingest_witness () : Append one "movie path" line per movie to this file. Diagnostic; writes nothing when unset.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0481651Z            --aggregate_only (false) : Regenerate the full dataset STAR/report from complete per-movie outputs; never process or rewrite a movie.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0482540Z        --only_do_unfinished (false) : Only run motion correction for those micrographs for which there is not yet an output micrograph.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0483559Z                   --do_at_most (-1) : Only process at most this number of (unprocessed) micrographs.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0484197Z              --grouping_for_ps (-1) : Group this number of frames and write summed power spectrum. -1 == do not write
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0484736Z                     --ps_size (512) : Output size of power spectrum
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0485173Z               --first_frame_sum (1) : First movie frame used in output sum (start at 1)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0485893Z               --last_frame_sum (-1) : Last movie frame used in output sum (0 or negative: use all)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0486611Z              --expected_frames (-1) : Expected decoded frames per movie (-1: unchecked; per-movie STAR count overrides this fallback)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0487183Z                 --eer_grouping (40) : EER grouping
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0487621Z                --eer_upsampling (1) : EER upsampling (1 = physical or 2 = 2x super-resolution)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0488044Z ====== MOTIONCOR2 options ===== 
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0488358Z            --use_motioncor2 (false) : Use Shawn Zheng's MOTIONCOR2.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0488970Z                 --motioncor2_exe () : Location of MOTIONCOR2 executable (or through RELION_MOTIONCOR2_EXECUTABLE environment variable)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0489581Z                    --bin_factor (1) : Binning factor (can be non-integer)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0490320Z                     --bfactor (150) : B-factor (in pix^2) that will be used inside MOTIONCOR2
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0491290Z                        --gainref () : Location of MRC file with the gain reference to be applied
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0492773Z                      --gain_rot (0) : Rotate the gain reference this number times 90 degrees clock-wise (in relion_display). This is same as MotionCor2's RotGain. 0, 1, 2 or 3
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0494910Z                     --gain_flip (0) : Flip the gain reference. This is same as MotionCor2's FlipGain. 0, 1 (flip Y == upside down) or 2 (flip X == left to right)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0496164Z                       --patch_x (1) : Patching in X-direction for MOTIONCOR2
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0496900Z                       --patch_y (1) : Patching in Y-direction for MOTIONCOR2
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0497869Z                  --group_frames (1) : Average together this many frames before calculating the beam-induced shifts
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0501081Z                    --defect_file () : Location of a MOTIONCOR2-style detector defect file or a defect map (1 means bad). A .txt defect file holds whitespace-separated integer quadruples (x y w h), conventionally one rectangle per line; comments, headers and a UTF-8 BOM are not supported. Blank lines are ignored, an empty file masks nothing, rectangles with width or height <= 0 are skipped, and rectangles are clipped to the image.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0504319Z                        --archive () : Location of the directory for archiving movies in 4-byte MRC format
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0505261Z            --even_odd_split (false) : Generate two images summed from odd and even movie frames. Later used for denoising in tomography.
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0506249Z          --other_motioncor2_args () : Additional arguments to MOTIONCOR2
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0507570Z                            --gpu () : Device ids. --use_motioncor2 passes the MotionCor2 list syntax through (e.g 0:1:2:3); --use_own supports exactly one device id (e.g 0) and rejects a list
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0508329Z ====== Dose-weighting options ===== 
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0508673Z            --dose_weighting (false) : Use dose-weighting scheme
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0509044Z                       --angpix (-1) : Pixel size in Angstroms
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0509410Z                      --voltage (-1) : Voltage (in kV) for dose-weighting
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0509883Z                --dose_per_frame (1) : Electron dose (in electrons/A2/frame) for dose-weighting
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0510406Z                   --preexposure (0) : Pre-exposure (in electrons/A2) for dose-weighting
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0510814Z ====== Own motion correction options ===== 
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0511190Z                   --use_own (false) : Use our own implementation of motion correction
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0511842Z                   --float16 (false) : Write in half-precision 16 bit floating point numbers (MRC mode 12), instead of 32 bit (MRC mode 0).
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0512496Z               --skip_defect (false) : Skip hot pixel detection
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0513244Z                          --seed (1) : Random seed for defect correction (default: 1 for reproducible runs)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0513950Z                 --save_noDW (false) : Save aligned but non dose weighted micrograph
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0514498Z                      --max_iter (5) : Maximum number of iterations for alignment. Only valid with --use_own
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0515025Z        --interpolate_shifts (false) : (EXPERIMENTAL) Interpolate shifts
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0515600Z                --ccf_downsample (0) : (EXPERT) Downsampling rate of CC map. default = 0 = automatic based on B factor
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0516394Z             --early_binning (false) : Do binning before alignment to reduce memory usage. This might dampen signal near Nyquist. (ON by default)
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0517025Z          --no_early_binning (false) : Disable --early_binning
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0517679Z      --dose_motionstats_cutoff (4.) : Electron dose (in electrons/A2) at which to distinguish early/late global accumulated motion in output statistics
2026-10-14T22:51:54.0518335Z                           --version : Print RELION version and exit
